text='# PFP prompts 22 through 31\n\nThe ordered ten prompts after the twenty-one previously completed nodes were executed locally through PFP with dedicated run/review folders, exact source snapshots, independent domain predicates, native Rust/Python agreement and literal named Lean reports. Every executed checkpoint retains an operad delta. P0 mining precedes P1; P2 gates precede P4/P5. Actual dependency/elaboration failures and their P3 successors remain sealed. No external provider was dispatched; active chat cost is unmeasured. This is one Codex researcher, not an independent-author panel.\n\n| Prompt | Supported step | Remaining obligation |\n|---|---|---|\n'+'\n'.join(table)+'\n\nReview corrected/fenced these specific source or composition issues:\n\n- The absolute-value p=1 rule has I3(1,1,-1)=2. An aligned positive triple gives0; that does not imply universal I3 vanishing. A new admitted-Real.rpow proof establishes the actual (3/5)^p+(4/5)^p=1 iff p=2 equation.\n- The source (N0,N1) basis coefficients A,B are distinct from embedding weights. Galois comparison is B=0, not A=B. Universal polynomial I3 vanishing is distinguished from a single zero triple.\n- Scalar K23 examples with objectives4/12 do not certify the matrix6/9/2 target. The actual six-edge diagonal defects, dual polar constraints, divergence, potentials, residuals and costs are retained. Formal full matrix/LP transport remains open, and no publication erratum is claimed.\n- Tsirelson uses two actual Q(sqrt2) SOS matrices and a normalized rational Bell density. Kernel rational quadratic-form proofs are separated from concrete real/matrix transport.\n- A Boolean report half-step obstruction coexists with unitary Q(i) amplitude roots. Mixed root signs yield negative swap, so the square-equals-swap graft carries a same-sign condition. Integer branch tags are not analytic logarithms.\n- Census lost/open labels are source-declared inputs, not newly inferred necessity verdicts. Quotient construction and positive metric rescaling are not field/model or full CPTP-norm uniqueness theorems.\n\nFresh compilation found absent E003/E005 modules imported by H000FinitePresentedCarrier. This batch adds new minimal report-fiber definitions and proofs, explicitly marked as new implementations rather than recovered historical sources. The difference codomain preserves the input pair and Zero tests supplied report equality, matching the actual H000 parity interface. Failed missing-module, setoid elaboration and initial codomain submissions remain retained; their numerical certificates are unchanged in the passing repair. No sorry/custom axiom passed acceptance.\n\nMeasured counts: '+json.dumps(counts,sort_keys=True)+'.\n\nFresh integration: '+json.dumps(integration,sort_keys=True)+'. Counts are unique tests/anchors, not sums of repeated gates. Pinned cached Mathlib is an import; neither a fresh full Mathlib build, full transitive dependency custody, whole-repository/hosted CI, physical reconstruction nor complete formal operad coherence is claimed. Full refined-carrier identity, substitution, symmetry and coherence proofs remain explicit obligations. The original prompts and historical source labels are unchanged.\n\nRead-only exact/custody replay (recomputes predicates and checks saved receipts, not fresh compiler runs):\n\n    py -3.9 -X utf8 verify_batch.py\n    py -3.9 -X utf8 -O verify_batch.py\n    py -3.9 -X utf8 test_custody_guards.py -v\n\nSource/candidate and artifact digests bind captured bytes, not independent authorship. tools/ retains local construction, repair, review, integration and staging scripts; initial runner and dependency-order versions are retained separately. GitHub merge status is verified independently of these artifacts. AuthorityEffect: None.\n'
